# Python environment (optisim)

This repo uses a **shared** virtual environment outside the workspace:

`/Users/mdovale/Work-local/__virtual-environments/optisim`

It provides **FINESSE 3** and **ZOSPy** (Zemax OpticStudio via ZOS-API). Do not create a new `venv/` in the repo unless the user explicitly asks.

## Commands

Always use the venv binaries (do not rely on bare `python`, `python3`, or `pip`):

```bash
/Users/mdovale/Work-local/__virtual-environments/optisim/bin/python
/Users/mdovale/Work-local/__virtual-environments/optisim/bin/pip
```

Or activate once per shell session, then run commands normally:

```bash
source /Users/mdovale/Work-local/__virtual-environments/optisim/bin/activate
```

## Agent shell runs

When running Python, pytest, pip, or notebooks in the terminal:

1. Prefer the full `.../optisim/bin/python` path, **or**
2. `source .../optisim/bin/activate` in the same command chain before other commands.

Example:

```bash
source /Users/mdovale/Work-local/__virtual-environments/optisim/bin/activate && python -m pytest
```

## ZOSPy note

ZOSPy needs a working .NET/Mono runtime and Zemax OpticStudio on the machine where it is imported. FINESSE does not. If `import zospy` fails locally, fix the host runtime; do not switch to a different Python environment.
